---
import Recording from "@/components/Recording.astro"
import CodeBlock from "@/components/CodeBlock.astro"
import DocsLayout from "@/layouts/DocsLayout.astro"
import { docsMetadata } from "@/lib/docs-meta"

const metadata = docsMetadata("/docs/cli/version")
---
<DocsLayout metadata={metadata}>
    <section>
      <h1 class="mt-0 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-4">gooze version</h1>
      <p class="gz-prose gz-prose--lead mb-8">You&apos;re filing a bug report or checking that an upgrade landed.{" "}<code>gooze version</code> prints the Gooze version and the Go version it was built with.</p>
      <div>
        <div id="usage">
          <h2>Usage</h2>
          <CodeBlock lang="bash" code="gooze version" />
          <p>The command takes no flags and prints one line on stdout: the module
            version and the Go version the binary was built with.{" "}<code>gooze --version</code> prints the same line (<code>v1.4.2+</code>).
            <code>-v</code> is not a short form of it: <code>-v</code> means <code>--verbose</code>.</p>
        </div>
        <div id="output">
          <h2>Example output</h2>
          <Recording name="calc-version" title="Recorded gooze version" />
          <p>The version comes from the Go build info, so a binary built from a
            local checkout instead of <code>go install ...@vX.Y.Z</code> shows{" "}<code>(devel)</code> in its place.</p>
        </div>
        <div id="why">
          <h2>Why this matters</h2>
          <p>Include this output in every bug report: it lets the team reproduce
            your issue against the exact build you ran. It is also the quickest
            way to confirm an upgrade landed after{" "}<code>go install</code> or a binary swap.</p>
        </div>
        <div id="ci">
          <h2>Pinning in CI</h2>
          <p>Log the version at the start of a CI job so mutation results are
            traceable to a specific gooze build, and fail fast if the pinned
            version drifts:</p>
          <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`gooze version
gooze version | grep -q 'gooze v1.4.1 ' || { echo 'unexpected gooze version'; exit 1; }`} />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
</DocsLayout>
